   "source": [
    "1. CURRENT STAGE: Bigram Model\n",
    "   Context Window (T) = 1 character. \n",
    "   Lookup logic: \"If current character is X, look up row X to guess the next character.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "2. NEXT UPGRADE: Bag of Words (The Bridge)\n",
    "   Context Window expands (T = 12). \n",
    "   Problem: How do we combine information from 12(block_size) characters?\n",
    "   Solution: We take a simple mathematical average of their rows. (Terrible because order is ignored).\n",
    "\n",
    "3. THE REVOLUTION: Self-Attention\n",
    "   Instead of a simple mathematical average, the tokens \"talk\" to each other.\n",
    "   Every token generates a \"Query\" (What I am looking for) and a \"Key\" (What I contain).\n",
    "   Tokens look back dynamically and calculate an attention score based on what matters most.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. THE POSITION PROBLEM: Positional Encodings\n",
    "   Self-Attention doesn't care about sequence order. \"The cat ate the fish\" looks identical to \"The fish ate the cat.\"\n",
    "   We add a fixed or learned positional vector directly to our embeddings to inject a sense of time/space.\n"
   ]
  },
