   "source": [
    "### Mathematical Trick | Intuition | Observation\n",
    "\n",
    "**In Principle:**  Our attention mechanism should be as such that they only influence upto the present token or timestep and not the timesteps ahead - i.e the present token semantics should only be influenced by the past tokens or timesteps. The Future timesteps or the next subsequent tokens that are yet to be predicted should not influence the present token..\n",
    "\n",
    "**Mathematical Observation:** We know that a Lower Triangular Matrix is the one that has all the elements above leading diagonal as 0. \n",
    "or as, \n",
    "L =  [a 0 0] \n",
    "     [b c 0]\n",
    "     [d e f]\n",
    "\n",
    "This shows that if the rows are the corresponding iterations - then for \n",
    "* 1st iteration, only the timestep= 0 can contribute to the attention for the particular token\n",
    "* 2nd iteration, only timestep = 0 and 1 can contribute to the attention for the particular target token\n",
    "* 3rd iteration, only timestep = 0,1 and 2 can contribute to the attention for the particular target token\n",
    "  .\n",
    "  .\n",
    "  .\n",
    "  and so on.\n",
    "\n",
    "This way we can consider only the timesteps <= target timestep in a Matrix Form.\n",
    "Moreover we need to average the summation of all previous timesteps out, therefore we can either \n",
    "* Do a Mat Mul of a lower triangular mat with the Embedding Matrix. This will give me the Attention for target tokens as modelled by timesteps before it at each iteration. Then average them.\n",
    "* Or Create a Normalized Lower Triangular Mat and then use it as the Multiplying Mat with the Embedding matrix to directly get averaged attention values \n"
   ]
